[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-337103"] :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x(1+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ then general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\nx(t)=C{e}^{-t}+f(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find the function $f(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x=-2t.\n$$\n\n*You may also wish to make use of the following result (constants omitted):*\n\n$$\n\\int t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t=(t-1){e}^{t}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nWe're told that, under the substitution ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ our d’Alembert differential equation transforms to the first-order linear equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x=-2t.\n$$\n\nWe'll solve this equation using the method of integrating factors. Since this equation is already of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nwe compute our integrating factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(t) & ={e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t}={e}^{\\int 1\\,\\text{d}t}={e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x{e}^{t} & =-2t{e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{t}) & =-2t{e}^{t} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x{e}^{t})\\,\\text{d}t & =-2\\int t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x{e}^{t} & =-2\\int t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x{e}^{t} & =-2(t-1){e}^{t}+C \\\\ x & =-2(t-1)+C{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\nx(t)=C{e}^{-t}+2-2t\n$$\n\nand finally, $f(t)=2-2t.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-337713/selection/51fe4d9f4931f07b92561d932efc8803695ea453516fd8a6992781fccfef8317" :answer/id #uuid "a9cf9071-00d3-5133-a88a-855276ec4eef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337713/selection/4f48fbd95469d031af9be5bfba787b9447795a914f4b1f81a50bc9862bea0370" :answer/id #uuid "e73d99ad-fe1e-55b3-a0de-42df6659388a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{t}^{2}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337713/selection/d205823a4afc53d31d9ac553351269ca8c026f36091cebf388aa3ebcf73946e4" :answer/id #uuid "1d60a7c8-96e8-56dd-bd87-8ef7d1c4139c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}+3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337713/selection/d7e88b3096b3f1163ae5e5c1d3fda1c14edb6d9b6ea13fc8f55c49de090a4b5b" :answer/id #uuid "8fd48a11-0606-5b9e-bf9d-a225d8a75e2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}-3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337713/selection/f017fe1ff73416171aff8b158c691401001dbcb027f3694a0fc15ed3409e0620" :answer/id #uuid "4ab3bb55-80be-52e5-afe1-afb0c53d566b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{t}^{2}-2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337713/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "899b4349-356f-5971-9e57-91f5f8794857" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337713/selection/d205823a4afc53d31d9ac553351269ca8c026f36091cebf388aa3ebcf73946e4" :answer-field/choices ["q-337713/selection/51fe4d9f4931f07b92561d932efc8803695ea453516fd8a6992781fccfef8317" "q-337713/selection/4f48fbd95469d031af9be5bfba787b9447795a914f4b1f81a50bc9862bea0370" "q-337713/selection/d205823a4afc53d31d9ac553351269ca8c026f36091cebf388aa3ebcf73946e4" "q-337713/selection/d7e88b3096b3f1163ae5e5c1d3fda1c14edb6d9b6ea13fc8f55c49de090a4b5b" "q-337713/selection/f017fe1ff73416171aff8b158c691401001dbcb027f3694a0fc15ed3409e0620"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337713" :question/id #uuid "3a284af2-f2f5-545e-967c-396326bd92f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-337713" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+3(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}).\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ then the general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\ny(t)=(\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-3t+C}{(t-1)^{2}})f(t)+g(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find $f(t)+g(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1}=\\frac{3}{t(1-t)}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nWe're told that, under the substitution ${y}^{′}(x)=t,$ our d’Alembert differential equation transforms to the first-order linear equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1}=\\frac{3}{t(1-t)}.\n$$\n\nWe'll solve this equation using the method of integrating factors. Since this equation is already of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nwe compute our integrating factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(t) & ={e}^{\\int P(t)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 2/(t-1)\\,\\text{d}t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t-1|} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =(t-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying our differential equation by $I(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+(t-1)^{2}\\frac{2x}{t-1} & =(t-1)^{2}\\frac{3}{t(1-t)} \\\\ (t-1)^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+2(t-1)x & =\\frac{3(1-t)}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRewriting the left-hand side as an exact derivative, and integrating both sides of the equation with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2}) & =\\frac{3(1-t)}{t} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x(t-1)^{2})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\frac{3(1-t)}{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x(t-1)^{2} & =\\int (\\frac{3}{t}-3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ x(t-1)^{2} & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-3t+C \\\\ x & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-3t+C}{(t-1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-3t+C}{(t-1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo recover $y$, we substitute $x$ into\n\n$$\ny=x{t}^{2}+3t,\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\ny(t)=(\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-3t+C}{(t-1)^{2}}){t}^{2}+3t.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $f(t)={t}^{2},\\,g(t)=3t,$ and\n\n$$\nf(t)+g(t)={t}^{2}+3t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-337713/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6bb3f2e-ee56-56f2-94f2-4b454a187ab7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337713"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365377/field-1/f1218c46d80d9fb5d0ce4e63a6990a209e06c934a8e8e582e82cb953fa842d0b" :answer/id #uuid "4e5d9760-69f2-54f2-8b47-51f37b331655" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{1-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365377/field-1/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" :answer/id #uuid "8c9da109-f78d-5916-9de7-fd197cef77af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365377/field-1/80bbd85e954c5ee13b7aeae440dd7768844017ba57489ce1faf7391ebeb97e37" :answer/id #uuid "8ae303e9-f2dd-5f6c-930a-5a55e61dfb3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2t}{t-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365377/field-1/c7ceb9c7f4281f7d474d2b565ab560d18188959bff80de8f97b53bc8f87be516" :answer/id #uuid "231d8aa8-7b20-5d21-a9b5-5778df6b262b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365377/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6916717-a837-5e89-99b4-2b8dd79841be" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365377/field-1/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-365377/field-1/f1218c46d80d9fb5d0ce4e63a6990a209e06c934a8e8e582e82cb953fa842d0b" "q-365377/field-1/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" "q-365377/field-1/80bbd85e954c5ee13b7aeae440dd7768844017ba57489ce1faf7391ebeb97e37" "q-365377/field-1/c7ceb9c7f4281f7d474d2b565ab560d18188959bff80de8f97b53bc8f87be516"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365377/field-2/03081fb08261b16cf14f608b0ebad6df9235297862154264c645e379d42ebed2" :answer/id #uuid "fe25f07b-4cdc-546d-af93-11cd7c61f206" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2t}{1-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365377/field-2/f1218c46d80d9fb5d0ce4e63a6990a209e06c934a8e8e582e82cb953fa842d0b" :answer/id #uuid "edb4f8bb-b895-5a35-9b74-430970a28bec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{1-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365377/field-2/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" :answer/id #uuid "6ddcc38f-9f21-5f3e-8d65-559f8bcc9f0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365377/field-2/1734c7b67516b1c7d4f6426859d3a27d3aea2302c54d5299c56f5a6b2463915f" :answer/id #uuid "e38e09e2-7e9e-5e13-b585-b1bd0a1611c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{-2t}{t-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365377/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a598d06-a28e-59fe-b294-70ceed87705a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365377/field-2/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-365377/field-2/03081fb08261b16cf14f608b0ebad6df9235297862154264c645e379d42ebed2" "q-365377/field-2/f1218c46d80d9fb5d0ce4e63a6990a209e06c934a8e8e582e82cb953fa842d0b" "q-365377/field-2/388369a331261df95722349c7a37305c2de365f4919903abb2b6d0032a3650dd" "q-365377/field-2/1734c7b67516b1c7d4f6426859d3a27d3aea2302c54d5299c56f5a6b2463915f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365377" :question/id #uuid "3a50d1c6-56ea-52b8-9b96-6b89c2e8b0cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-365377" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation, defined for $t>0:$\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}-{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}\n$$\n\nUsing the substitution $t=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ the equation can be transformed to a first-order linear equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the functions $P$ and $Q.$\n\n$\\,\\,P(t)=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,Q(t)=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nIn our case, we wish to transform the equation\n\n$$\ny=x{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}-{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}\n$$\n\ninto a first-order linear equation for $x=x(t).$ We proceed in three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Substitute, and differentiate with respect to $x.$\n\nWe have the substitution\n\n$$\nt=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=x{t}^{2}-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating both sides with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x{t}^{2}-{t}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum and product rules and using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x{t}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({t}^{2}) \\\\ t & ={t}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({t}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({t}^{2}) \\\\ t & ={t}^{2}+2xt\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}-2t\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Isolate the derivative and take its reciprocal.\n\nWe isolate $\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-{t}^{2} & =2xt\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}-2t\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ t(1-t) & =(2xt-2t)\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{t(1-t)}{2xt-2t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{t(1-t)}{2xt-2t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by taking the reciprocal of each side, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{2xt-2t}{t(1-t)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Express the derivative as a first-order linear equation.\n\nFinally, we write this in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{2xt-2t}{t(1-t)} \\\\ t(1-t)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =2xt-2t \\\\ t(1-t)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-2xt & =-2t \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{2xt}{t(1-t)} & =\\frac{-2t}{t(1-t)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\frac{2x}{1-t} & =\\frac{-2}{1-t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2x}{t-1} & =\\frac{2}{t-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{2}{t-1},\\,Q(t)=\\frac{2}{t-1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-365377/field-1" "q-365377/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "126ffd6c-f5a9-564f-935f-398a126d2cbd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365377"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365387/field-1/8899a073a0829eca9329c729b69ea6d2e3da486d939e7aefa8443c866ee5b86c" :answer/id #uuid "d474c916-6a2f-5917-b857-397f6148a0bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{t}{{t}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365387/field-1/dae588f88bd514761e3fb9fd827644457a28699e1223aa1630d9e12efca5defa" :answer/id #uuid "800dc784-be71-5041-b8b5-b4540252b066" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365387/field-1/12e89494e4449d07c60b85624fcccbe20b1e6a8e50b5c85a7690b33c90d52b00" :answer/id #uuid "e52c7e35-94a8-544c-a5a7-1b301ecd1cf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t({t}^{2}-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365387/field-1/30e90459817c165b1c63b6207126bf30e17ca68ced82d2ed2d017525a7dffd69" :answer/id #uuid "083233ed-af9f-5c56-b2a8-cfa5a625abb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}({t}^{2}-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365387/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac0270fd-fa92-5fba-a6ec-1f8c96668b29" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365387/field-1/12e89494e4449d07c60b85624fcccbe20b1e6a8e50b5c85a7690b33c90d52b00" :answer-field/choices ["q-365387/field-1/8899a073a0829eca9329c729b69ea6d2e3da486d939e7aefa8443c866ee5b86c" "q-365387/field-1/dae588f88bd514761e3fb9fd827644457a28699e1223aa1630d9e12efca5defa" "q-365387/field-1/12e89494e4449d07c60b85624fcccbe20b1e6a8e50b5c85a7690b33c90d52b00" "q-365387/field-1/30e90459817c165b1c63b6207126bf30e17ca68ced82d2ed2d017525a7dffd69"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365387/field-2/12e89494e4449d07c60b85624fcccbe20b1e6a8e50b5c85a7690b33c90d52b00" :answer/id #uuid "415df2c8-c131-57ac-934c-e704f3a61221" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t({t}^{2}-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365387/field-2/8899a073a0829eca9329c729b69ea6d2e3da486d939e7aefa8443c866ee5b86c" :answer/id #uuid "f98762c7-7ebe-510b-8b4a-c4261cea0546" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{t}{{t}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365387/field-2/dae588f88bd514761e3fb9fd827644457a28699e1223aa1630d9e12efca5defa" :answer/id #uuid "fa738fda-cc93-5997-bb1c-5777ab17803d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365387/field-2/123922ffb2a3f3556cd9bba9ef948b09977a0d9ad6e77786eb32d53e00dfa916" :answer/id #uuid "c9c3def1-f853-5180-9387-46dea8763528" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{2}}{{t}^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365387/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "336e1045-ab96-578b-a2fe-67430bf170bd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365387/field-2/8899a073a0829eca9329c729b69ea6d2e3da486d939e7aefa8443c866ee5b86c" :answer-field/choices ["q-365387/field-2/12e89494e4449d07c60b85624fcccbe20b1e6a8e50b5c85a7690b33c90d52b00" "q-365387/field-2/8899a073a0829eca9329c729b69ea6d2e3da486d939e7aefa8443c866ee5b86c" "q-365387/field-2/dae588f88bd514761e3fb9fd827644457a28699e1223aa1630d9e12efca5defa" "q-365387/field-2/123922ffb2a3f3556cd9bba9ef948b09977a0d9ad6e77786eb32d53e00dfa916"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365387" :question/id #uuid "01283c40-bda7-59b4-8f16-b320c423d254" :question/math-academy-id "q-365387" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x\\cdot \\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the substitution $t=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ the equation can be transformed to a first-order linear equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the functions $P$ and $Q.$\n\n$\\,\\,P(t)=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,Q(t)=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nIn our case, we wish to transform the equation\n\n$$\ny=x\\cdot \\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\ninto a first-order linear equation for $x=x(t).$ We proceed in three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Substitute, and differentiate with respect to $x.$\n\nWe have the substitution\n\n$$\nt=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=x\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}+t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating both sides with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}+t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum and product rules and using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\cdot \\frac{1}{t})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(t) \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{t}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{t})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(t) \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{t}-\\frac{x}{{t}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Isolate the derivative and take its reciprocal.\n\nWe isolate $\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-\\frac{1}{t} & =-\\frac{x}{{t}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{{t}^{2}-1}{t} & =(\\frac{{t}^{2}-x}{{t}^{2}})\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{t({t}^{2}-1)}{{t}^{2}-x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{t({t}^{2}-1)}{{t}^{2}-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by taking the reciprocal of each side, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{{t}^{2}-x}{t({t}^{2}-1)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Express the derivative as a first-order linear equation.\n\nFinally, we write this in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{{t}^{2}-x}{t({t}^{2}-1)} \\\\ t({t}^{2}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & ={t}^{2}-x \\\\ t({t}^{2}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x & ={t}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{x}{t({t}^{2}-1)} & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{t({t}^{2}-1)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{x}{t({t}^{2}-1)} & =\\frac{t}{{t}^{2}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{1}{t({t}^{2}-1)},\\,Q(t)=\\frac{t}{{t}^{2}-1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-365387/field-1" "q-365387/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "126ffd6c-f5a9-564f-935f-398a126d2cbd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365387"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365388/field-1/e6234e94a6950ba604c21415fc414d6e044d6a6871bcd9af6da9461ed13295ff" :answer/id #uuid "a4b05134-5a34-56d8-9a7c-0ee32b95e891" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365388/field-1/5f39a165dcd4e2cebb6b2f1fda2f8833028c2ba08984efd1d216c50ddc35b90b" :answer/id #uuid "a8b29b12-196a-5f04-b57f-023fc0d9618c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{14t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365388/field-1/e554b2d1a829e3023f2f5c58be4a2f5d00205f48867c9eff7f272eb00265c3ca" :answer/id #uuid "9ad7e0ac-f228-5b80-8c9e-b23199723802" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365388/field-1/7a9b2fe9b7a37bd34d2ff7460544864298cbb4cd533621118ecc3b9990c4e5a1" :answer/id #uuid "98bf05a3-c66d-59b2-b87f-f6ea0a8e00ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}{t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365388/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ab3c536-60ee-51bb-8bb8-5aa71b503d72" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365388/field-1/e6234e94a6950ba604c21415fc414d6e044d6a6871bcd9af6da9461ed13295ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-365388/field-1/e6234e94a6950ba604c21415fc414d6e044d6a6871bcd9af6da9461ed13295ff" "q-365388/field-1/5f39a165dcd4e2cebb6b2f1fda2f8833028c2ba08984efd1d216c50ddc35b90b" "q-365388/field-1/e554b2d1a829e3023f2f5c58be4a2f5d00205f48867c9eff7f272eb00265c3ca" "q-365388/field-1/7a9b2fe9b7a37bd34d2ff7460544864298cbb4cd533621118ecc3b9990c4e5a1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365388/field-2/a79adc22257edf32e140d6eb0f1995388732134af687371a157e409662400672" :answer/id #uuid "8db55f49-231d-5ee7-b81e-beaf4a8458e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14t}{t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365388/field-2/b3a5aa7d35816f4ab11d4f64957aa86f5538d22079c78cb253e517babbf7a62e" :answer/id #uuid "6e1d86c5-473e-590e-8184-fc3a80f2c10c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{t}{t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365388/field-2/86009619693bc2eeb17e41a527e5dc80bee8e3f2fe3680612edcc096897cde90" :answer/id #uuid "225de4f0-d43b-546b-af62-85d68e57d802" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14t}{t+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365388/field-2/a07a29e67b82f45cc13c5f3de0e7ffb26aa7d1d855a15618dd2038d1f6a06c3e" :answer/id #uuid "3fcdb8c7-473c-58bb-9315-f70cf0424d8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{14}{t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365388/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "147d7bc2-0295-5d78-aac0-4d49bd0215bd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-365388/field-2/a79adc22257edf32e140d6eb0f1995388732134af687371a157e409662400672" :answer-field/choices ["q-365388/field-2/a79adc22257edf32e140d6eb0f1995388732134af687371a157e409662400672" "q-365388/field-2/b3a5aa7d35816f4ab11d4f64957aa86f5538d22079c78cb253e517babbf7a62e" "q-365388/field-2/86009619693bc2eeb17e41a527e5dc80bee8e3f2fe3680612edcc096897cde90" "q-365388/field-2/a07a29e67b82f45cc13c5f3de0e7ffb26aa7d1d855a15618dd2038d1f6a06c3e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365388" :question/id #uuid "eba8e4b2-801e-5880-a5da-71fbafe7b623" :question/math-academy-id "q-365388" :question/problem "Consider the d’Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=3xcos\\,(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})+7{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the substitution $t=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ the equation can be transformed to a first-order linear equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the functions $P$ and $Q.$\n\n$\\,\\,P(t)=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,Q(t)=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nIn our case, we wish to transform the equation\n\n$$\ny=3xcos\\,(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})+7{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}\n$$\n\ninto a first-order linear equation for $x=x(t).$ We proceed in three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Substitute, and differentiate with respect to $x.$\n\nWe have the substitution\n\n$$\nt=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+7{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating both sides with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+7{t}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum and product rules and using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7{t}^{2}) \\\\ t & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+3x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7{t}^{2}) \\\\ t & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}+14t\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Isolate the derivative and take its reciprocal.\n\nWe isolate $\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & =-3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}+14t\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & =(14t-3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}{14t-3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)} & =\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}t}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}{14t-3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by taking the reciprocal of each side, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{14t-3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Express the derivative as a first-order linear equation.\n\nFinally, we write this in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+P(t)x=Q(t)\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{14t-3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)} \\\\ (t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =14t-3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ (t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & =14t \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)} & =\\frac{14t}{t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)}{t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)},\\,Q(t)=\\frac{14t}{t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-365388/field-1" "q-365388/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "126ffd6c-f5a9-564f-935f-398a126d2cbd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365388"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
